    "note": "ECS4120 Series datasheet R16 (EC-DS-0324-R16, 2024-03-12) prints 128 Gbps switching capacity and 95 Mpps for both fibre members; a combo position carries one medium at a time, so its 1G counts once. https://www.edge-core.com/download/ecs4120-series-ds-r16/?wpdmdl=1696"
  },
  "notes": "Port census from ECS4120 Series datasheet R16 (EC-DS-0324-R16, 2024-03-12) (https://www.edge-core.com/download/ecs4120-series-ds-r16/?wpdmdl=1696): 100/1000BASE-X SFP ports 20, Combo Gigabit (RJ-45/SFP) ports 4, SFP+ 10 Gigabit uplink ports 4, GE out-of-band management port Yes, RJ-45 console port 1. The CLI reference fixes both ends of the numbering - \"Ports 1-24 (1000BASE SFP) support 1000sfp or 100fx\" and \"Ports 25-28 (10G SFP+) support 1000sfp\" (https://www.edge-core.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/ECS4120-Series_CLI-R06_20251014.pdf) - so the 20 fibre ports are Eth 1/1-20 and the four 10G uplinks Eth 1/25-28; the four combo positions are written as the 21-24 positions that remain, following the datasheet port order of 20 SFP then 4 combo. Edgecore prints no full 28F port map, so that placement is the one part of this census read from order rather than from a printed per-port list. Flash 256 MB, DRAM 512 MB, MAC table 16 K, jumbo 9 KB, max system power 60 W, 44 x 22 x 4.4 cm, 3.32 kg, 100-240 VAC plus a -48 to -60 VDC input, dying gasp supported (28Fv2 members only). Each combo pair is two ports sharing one position (comboWith / comboRole), the RJ-45 side at 10/100/1000 and the SFP side at 100/1000, as the datasheet prints. No PoE. Software ECS4120 FW V1.2.2.30, posted with the ECS4120 series R16 datasheet on the product download list."
}
